  "definitions": {
    "rule": "within each category, Scenario:k of the deposit is the k-th scenario of data/derived/kept901_5feat+elec10.csv in ascending order of (Model, Scenario), code-point order",
    "equal": "largest absolute deviation over the nine decades 2020-2100 at most 1e-06 of the deposited variable's largest absolute value in the category, on each of the sixteen variables",
    "duplicates": "deposited scenarios whose values coincide on all compared variables and decades: every value differs by at most 1e-06 of the variable's largest absolute value in the deposit (members of a group must agree to 1e-09); groups are sets of scenarios connected by such pairs. The groups on the fifteen variables of the D9 rule are checked against the column duplicate_group of data/derived/x5_folds_901.csv, which 09_model_groups.py derives from the AR6 values. Kyoto Gases are not among the fifteen: their deviation inside a group is the largest absolute difference between a member and the group's first, as a share of the variable's largest absolute value (identical: at most 1e-09)"
  },
